nt :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314455} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2e9fe0-9d14-5584-9191-0594a5f5e62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312337} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9fe0aa-cdb6-5e9b-95ba-83e767629260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f9fe0aa-cdb6-5e9b-95ba-83e767629260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312621} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3422fc-9101-5049-b9da-89d0ec0f636d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7b4ca9-d4f5-5b81-8dfc-3c846dff159a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312298} {:answer/id #uuid "352fdb5e-5751-5d23-aed4-b0c4585bee5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312402} {:answer/id #uuid "5867f2da-f584-5b0e-ac8e-bbe3cffb4923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312683} {:answer/id #uuid "9a599ed7-aafe-501d-b364-42c43da7d22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "352fdb5e-5751-5d23-aed4-b0c4585bee5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312402} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2b9423-79f0-5dc9-ab2c-4fbd6f9e2d00" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81480660-8b23-5d75-8411-ad962650246b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339876" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+4y=3{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{-x})^{′}=-{e}^{-x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(-{e}^{-x})^{′}={e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n({e}^{-x})+5(-{e}^{-x})+4({e}^{-x})=3{e}^{-x}.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x{e}^{-x})^{′}={e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =({e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x})^{′}=-2{e}^{-x}+x{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(-2{e}^{-x}+x{e}^{-x})+5({e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x})+4(x{e}^{-x})=3{e}^{-x}.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x}$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x}+x{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640be27-8277-5a9c-bf14-83bcc7a38604" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of Inhomogeneous ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3594a392-68f2-5a5a-ad28-aa038b74bd73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149943} {:answer/id #uuid "91a0180e-f4e9-5fbb-991e-1010a5619806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3594a392-68f2-5a5a-ad28-aa038b74bd73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149943} :answer-field/id #uuid "43104a38-5959-58d8-9496-90b83dbb174c" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e1094b3-fc43-5250-9d6a-7b7ef61f3d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149945} {:answer/id #uuid "c18bc512-f9f7-5d52-9207-8a9c53bca94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/re